* [[Alan Tudyk]] as [[Mr. Nobody (comics)|Eric Morden / Mr. Nobody]] (season 1): An omnipresent supervillain capable of traveling through dimensions and altering reality. Aware of being in a television series because of his abilities, he often [[breaking the fourth wall|breaks the fourth wall]] and manipulates events through his narration.<ref name="Tudyk">{{cite web |last1=Andreeva |first1=Nellie |title=''Doom Patrol'': Alan Tudyk Cast as Mr. Nobody in DC Universe TV Series |url=https://deadline.com/2018/08/doom-patrol-alan-tudyk-cast-mr-nobody-eric-morden-dc-universe-tv-series-1202455285/ |website=Deadline Hollywood |access-date=August 31, 2018 |date=August 31, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180831184143/https://deadline.com/2018/08/doom-patrol-alan-tudyk-cast-mr-nobody-eric-morden-dc-universe-tv-series-1202455285/ |archive-date=August 31, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Ed Asner]] portrays Mr. Nobody in his hospital patient disguise.
* [[Matt Bomer]] and Matthew Zuk as [[Negative Man|Larry Trainor / Negative Man]]: A former [[United States Air Force]] pilot with a negative energy entity living inside him. Disfigured from the plane crash that ensued when he made contact with the negative spirit, he is covered in special bandages to prevent the spread of the radioactivity emanating from his body. Bomer voices the character and appears as Larry without bandages, while Zuk physically portrays the bandaged Larry.<ref name="Bomer">{{cite web |last1=Andreeva |first1=Nellie |title=''Doom Patrol'': Matt Bomer to Star as Negative Man in DC Universe TV Series |url=https://deadline.com/2018/10/doom-patrol-matt-bomer-star-negative-man-dc-universe-tv-series-1202475606/ |website=Deadline Hollywood |access-date=October 3, 2018 |date=October 3, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181004032311/https://deadline.com/2018/10/doom-patrol-matt-bomer-star-negative-man-dc-universe-tv-series-1202475606/ |archive-date=October 4, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> Braxton Alexander portrays Larry as a child.
