==Production==
===Development===
''Doom Patrol'' was announced in May 2018, as an intended spin-off of ''[[Titans (2018 TV series)|Titans]]'' for [[video on demand]] service [[DC Universe (streaming service)|DC Universe]] after co-creator and executive producer [[Geoff Johns]] revealed that ''Titans''{{'}} fourth episode would feature and be titled after the [[Doom Patrol]].<ref name="ew.com">{{cite magazine |url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/02/10/titans-the-doom-patrol/ |title=''Titans'' producer confirms The Doom Patrol for live-action series |last=Romano |first=Nick |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |date=February 10, 2018 |access-date=July 17, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180710073127/http://ew.com/tv/2018/02/10/titans-the-doom-patrol/ |archive-date=July 10, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> Despite the initial order and sharing characters and actors, however, ''Doom Patrol'' occupies a separate continuity from ''Titans''.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ksitetv.com/doom-patrol/interview-april-bowlby-talks-doom-patrol-titans-connections-more/189022/ |title=Interview: April Bowlby Talks ''Doom Patrol'', ''Titans'' Connections & More |first=Craig |last=Byrne |website=KsiteTV |date=February 13, 2019 |access-date=June 28, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115212006/http://www.ksitetv.com/doom-patrol/interview-april-bowlby-talks-doom-patrol-titans-connections-more/189022/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://collider.com/doom-patrol-jeremy-carver-interview/ |title=''Doom Patrol'' EP Jeremy Carver on Casting, Donkeys, and Supervillain Cockroaches |first=Christina |last=Radish |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]] |date=February 15, 2019 |access-date=June 28, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115211926/https://collider.com/doom-patrol-jeremy-carver-interview/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/dc-universes-doom-patrol-will-introduce-celsius-lodestone-beard-hunter-more-tca-2019/ |title=DC Universe's ''Doom Patrol'' Will Introduce Celsius, Lodestone, Beard Hunter & More [TCA 2019] |first=Fred |last=Topel |date=February 10, 2019 |website=[[/Film]] |access-date=June 28, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115211945/https://www.slashfilm.com/dc-universes-doom-patrol-will-introduce-celsius-lodestone-beard-hunter-more-tca-2019/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Fifteen episodes were developed for the first season, which premiered on February 15, 2019, and concluded on May 24. [[Jeremy Carver]] wrote the pilot, and served as an executive producer alongside Johns, [[Greg Berlanti]], and [[Sarah Schechter (producer)|Sarah Schechter]]. Production companies involved with the series include [[Berlanti Productions]] and [[Warner Bros. Television]].<ref name="SeriesOrder">{{cite web |last1=Petski |first1=Denise |title=''Doom Patrol'' Live-Action Drama Series from Greg Berlanti Greenlighted by DC Universe |url=https://deadline.com/2018/05/doom-patrol-live-action-drama-series-greg-berlanti-order-dc-universe-1202390689/ |website=Deadline Hollywood |access-date=May 14, 2018 |date=May 14, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180514215255/http://deadline.com/2018/05/doom-patrol-live-action-drama-series-greg-berlanti-order-dc-universe-1202390689/ |archive-date=May 14, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Variety Order">{{cite web |last1=Otterson |first1=Joe |title=DC Universe Orders Live-Action ''Doom Patrol'' Series With Greg Berlanti, Geoff Johns Producing |url=https://variety.com/2018/tv/news/doom-patrol-series-dc-universe-greg-berlanti-geoff-johns-1202809883/ |website=Variety |access-date=May 14, 2018 |date=May 14, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180514220111/http://variety.com/2018/tv/news/doom-patrol-series-dc-universe-greg-berlanti-geoff-johns-1202809883/ |archive-date=May 14, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="HR Order">{{cite web |last1=Goldberg |first1=Lesley |title=''Doom Patrol'' Live-Action Series From Greg Berlanti Set at DC Digital Service |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/doom-patrol-live-action-series-greg-berlanti-set-at-dc-digital-service-1111715 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |access-date=May 14, 2018 |date=May 14, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180515023357/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/doom-patrol-live-action-series-greg-berlanti-set-at-dc-digital-service-1111715 |archive-date=May 15, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> The series is influenced by writer [[Grant Morrison]]'s run of the comic.<ref name="Forbes">{{cite web |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/robsalkowitz/2019/03/26/ok-we-need-to-talk-about-doom-patrol/ |title=OK, We Need To Talk About ''Doom Patrol'' |first=Rob |last=Salkowitz |website=[[Forbes]] |date=May 26, 2019 |access-date=May 30, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115212027/https://www.forbes.com/sites/robsalkowitz/2019/03/26/ok-we-need-to-talk-about-doom-patrol/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

The second season premiered on both DC Universe and [[WarnerMedia]]'s video on demand service [[HBO Max]] on June 25, 2020.<ref name="S2 DH">{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2019/07/doom-patrol-renewed-season-2-dc-universe-hbo-max-1202649770/ |title=''Doom Patrol'' Renewed For Season 2 By DC Universe Via Deal With HBO Max – Comic-Con |last=Petski |first=Denise |website=Deadline Hollywood |date=July 20, 2019 |access-date=July 21, 2019 |archive-date=July 21, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190721031811/https://deadline.com/2019/07/doom-patrol-renewed-season-2-dc-universe-hbo-max-1202649770/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="S2 GameSpot">{{cite web |url=https://www.gamespot.com/articles/doom-patrol-gets-season-2-renewal-with-a-twist-tit/1100-6468580/ |title=''Doom Patrol'' Gets Season 2 Renewal with a Twist, ''Titans'' Gets Premiere Date |website=[[GameSpot]] |first=Chris E. |last=Haynee |date=July 25, 2019 |access-date=July 27, 2019 |archive-date=July 27, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190727164632/https://www.gamespot.com/amp-articles/doom-patrol-gets-season-2-renewal-with-a-twist-tit/1100-6468580/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Goldberg">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/hbo-max-schedules-second-wave-original-programming-1294403|title=HBO Max Schedules Second Wave of Original Programming|date=May 13, 2020|website=The Hollywood Reporter|first=Lesley|last=Goldberg|access-date=May 13, 2020|archive-date=November 15, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115211943/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/hbo-max-schedules-second-wave-original-programming-1294403|url-status=live}}</ref> The season was originally intended to have 10 episodes, but due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]], production was shut down before the 10th episode could be completed and the season instead comprised nine episodes.<ref name="10Episodes">{{cite web |last1=Acuna |first1=Kirsten |title='Doom Patrol' actress says season 2 was supposed to have one more episode, but they never finished filming because of the pandemic |url=https://www.insider.com/doom-patrol-season-2-10-episodes-2020-7 |website=[[Insider, Inc.]] |access-date=July 16, 2020 |date=July 9, 2020}}</ref> The third and a fourth season were later released on [[HBO Max]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2021/10/doom-patrol-renewed-for-season-4-at-hbo-max-1234856832/|title='Doom Patrol' Renewed For Season 4 At HBO Max|website=Deadline Hollywood|first=Peter|last=White|date=October 16, 2021|access-date=October 16, 2021|archive-date=October 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211016185724/https://deadline.com/2021/10/doom-patrol-renewed-for-season-4-at-hbo-max-1234856832/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Turchiano |first=Danielle |date=September 12, 2020 |title='Doom Patrol' Renewed for Season 3 at HBO Max |url=https://variety.com/2020/tv/news/doom-patrol-season-3-renewal-hbo-max-1234767034/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200912211446/https://variety.com/2020/tv/news/doom-patrol-season-3-renewal-hbo-max-1234767034/ |archive-date=September 12, 2020 |access-date=September 12, 2020 |website=Variety |language=en}}</ref> with the fourth being the final season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2023/01/titans-amp-doom-patrol-canceled-end-seasons-4-hbo-max-1235241013/|title='Titans' & 'Doom Patrol' To End With Seasons 4 On HBO Max|website=Deadline Hollywood|first=Nellie|last=Andreeva|date=January 25, 2023|access-date=January 26, 2023|archive-date=January 26, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230126011016/https://deadline.com/2023/01/titans-amp-doom-patrol-canceled-end-seasons-4-hbo-max-1235241013/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Casting===
The casting for ''Doom Patrol''{{'}}s first season was rounded up between July and October 2018. [[April Bowlby]], [[Brendan Fraser]], and [[Matt Bomer]] were cast as [[Elasti-Girl|Rita Farr]], the voice of [[Robotman (Cliff Steele)|Cliff Steele]], and the voice of [[Negative Man|Larry Trainor]], respectively, after being cast as the characters for guest appearances in ''Titans''.<ref name="Bowlby" /><ref name="ElastiGirl">{{cite magazine |url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/02/20/titans-casts-drop-dead-diva-star-as-elasti-girl/ |title=''Titans'' casts ''Drop Dead Diva'' star as Elasti-Girl |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |date=February 20, 2018 |access-date=February 21, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180220231122/http://ew.com/tv/2018/02/20/titans-casts-drop-dead-diva-star-as-elasti-girl/ |archive-date=February 20, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Diane Guerrero]] was cast as [[Crazy Jane|Jane]].<ref name="Guerrero" /><ref name="Bowlby" /> [[Joivan Wade]] was cast as [[Cyborg (DC Comics)|Victor "Vic" Stone / Cyborg]],<ref name="Wade" /> [[Alan Tudyk]] was cast as [[Mr. Nobody (comics)|Eric Morden / Mr. Nobody]],<ref name="Tudyk" /> and Riley Shanahan was cast to physically portray the cyborg version of Cliff.<ref name="Fraser" /> [[Timothy Dalton]] was cast as [[Chief (DC Comics)|Niles Caulder / Chief]]<ref name="Dalton" /> and Matthew Zuk was cast to physically portray the bandage-covered Larry.<ref name="Bomer" /> In March 2019, [[Mark Sheppard]] was cast as [[Willoughby Kipling]].<ref name="Sheppard">{{cite web |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/news/doom-patrol-cast-supernatural-mark-sheppard/ |title=''Doom Patrol'' Casts ''Supernatural'' Star Mark Sheppard |first=Charlie |last=Ridgely |website=Comicbook.com |date=March 4, 2019 |access-date=March 8, 2019 |archive-date=March 8, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190308081130/https://comicbook.com/dc/amp/2019/03/04/doom-patrol-cast-supernatural-mark-sheppard/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cbr.com/doom-patrol-marc-sheppard-willoughby-kipling/ |website=[[Comic Book Resources]] |title=''Supernatural Alum'' Joins ''Doom Patrol'' as John Constantine-esque Character |first=Noah |last=Dominguez |date=March 1, 2019 |access-date=March 2, 2019 |archive-date=March 2, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190302130903/https://www.cbr.com/doom-patrol-marc-sheppard-willoughby-kipling/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

In January 2020, Roger Floyd was cast as Red Jack, a malevolent entity, in the series' second season.<ref name="floyd">{{cite web |last=Campbell |first=Jacob |title=Roger Floyd To Play Red Jack In ''Doom Patrol'' Season 2 |url=https://fullcirclecinema.com/2020/01/20/roger-floyd-red-jack-doom-patrol/ |website=Full Circle Cinema |date=January 20, 2020 |access-date=February 9, 2020 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115212015/https://fullcirclecinema.com/2020/01/20/roger-floyd-red-jack-doom-patrol/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Other second-season castings that February included Abi Monterey as the Chief's superpowered daughter, [[Dorothy Spinner]],<ref name="shapiro">{{cite web |last1=Swift |first1=Andy |title=Doom Patrol Season 2: Meet The Chief's Powerful, Mysterious Daughter Dorothy |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/doom-patrol-season-2-dorothy-cast-abigail-shapiro-chief-daughter-1155632/ |website=TVLine |access-date=February 8, 2020 |date=February 5, 2020 |archive-date=February 5, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200205183407/https://tvline.com/2020/02/05/doom-patrol-season-2-dorothy-cast-abigail-shapiro-chief-daughter/ |url-status=live}}</ref> and Karen Obilom as Roni Evers, a military veteran with a mysterious past who Vic meets while attending a PTSD support group.<ref name="obilom">{{cite web |url=https://deadline.com/2020/02/karen-obilom-doom-patrol-elizabeth-bowen-resident-alien-1202857991/ |title=Karen Obilom Joins ''Doom Patrol''; Elizabeth Bowen Books ''Resident Alien'' |website=Deadline Hollywood |first=Denise |last=Petski |date=February 12, 2020 |access-date=February 12, 2020 |archive-date=February 12, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200212234907/https://deadline.com/2020/02/karen-obilom-doom-patrol-elizabeth-bowen-resident-alien-1202857991/ |url-status=live}}</ref> [[Samantha Marie Ware]] was cast as one of [[Crazy Jane#Personalities|Jane's identities]] in March,<ref name="ware">{{cite web |url=https://www.cbr.com/doom-patrol-casts-samantha-ware-season-2/ |title=''Doom Patrol'': ''Glee'' Alum Samantha Ware Cast In Season 2 |website=CBR |last=Galanis |first=Evangelina |date=March 8, 2020 |access-date=March 9, 2020 |archive-date=June 20, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200620062214/https://www.cbr.com/doom-patrol-casts-samantha-ware-season-2/ |url-status=live}}</ref> later revealed to be the former primary identity Miranda. [[Michelle Gomez]] was cast as [[Madame Rouge]], a new series regular for the third season in March 2021.<ref name="MichelleG">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2021/03/doom-patrol-michelle-gomez-madame-rouge-season-3-dc-1234711382/|title=''Doom Patrol'': Michelle Gomez Joins Season 3 as Series Regular, Will Play Madame Rouge|website=Deadline Hollywood|first1=Alexandra|last1=Del Rosario|date=March 10, 2021|access-date=March 10, 2021|archive-date=March 10, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210310194441/https://deadline.com/2021/03/doom-patrol-michelle-gomez-madame-rouge-season-3-dc-1234711382/|url-status=live}}</ref> In April, [[Sebastian Croft]] and [[Ty Tennant]] were cast as the Dead Boy Detectives.<ref name="DeadBoyDetectives">{{cite web|url=https://thedirect.com/article/doom-patrol-season-3-cast-sebastian-croft-ty-tennant-dead-boy-detectives-exclusive|title=Doom Patrol Season 3: Sebastian Croft & Ty Tennant Cast as Dead Boy Detectives (Exclusive)|website=The Direct|first1=Aeron Mer|last1=Del Eclarinal|date=April 15, 2021|access-date=April 16, 2021|archive-date=April 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210416021929/https://thedirect.com/article/doom-patrol-season-3-cast-sebastian-croft-ty-tennant-dead-boy-detectives-exclusive|url-status=live}}</ref> Later that month Micah Joe Parker, [[Wynn Everett]], [[Miles Mussenden]], Anita Kalathara and Gina Hiraizumi were cast as members of the Sisterhood of Dada, while Madalyn Horcher was cast as a guest in connection with [[Sebastian Croft]] and [[Ty Tennant]].<ref name="S3Recurring">{{cite web|last=Del Rosario|first=Alexandra|title='Doom Patrol': HBO Max Adds Five In Recurring Roles To Season 3 Cast|url=https://deadline.com/2021/04/doom-patrol-hbo-max-five-recur-season-3-1234742555/|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=April 23, 2021|access-date=April 23, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.superherohype.com/tv/496618-doom-patrol-season-3-casts-eight-new-characters|title=Doom Patrol Season 3 Casts Eight New Characters|last=Abbate|first=Jake|website=SuperHeroHype|date=April 23, 2021|access-date=April 23, 2021}}</ref> In September 2022, [[Madeline Zima]] was cast as [[Casey Brinke]] for the fourth season,<ref name="MadelineZ">{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/tv/fall-tv-preview-november-december-premieres/|title=What to expect from ''Doom Patrol'', ''Irreverent'', ''Slow Horses'', and more shows coming later this year|magazine=Entertainment Weekly|author=EW Staff|date=September 23, 2022|access-date=October 17, 2022}}</ref> while [[Sendhil Ramamurthy]] joined the cast as Mr. 104 in a recurring capacity for the fourth season in October.<ref name="SendhilR">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/doom-patrol-season-4-sendhil-ramamurthy-mr-104-1234887633/|title=Sendhil Ramamurthy to Battle the ''Doom Patrol'' as [Spoiler] in Season 4|work=TVLine|first=Andy|last=Swift|date=October 17, 2022|access-date=October 17, 2022}}</ref>

===Filming===
Principal photography for the first season began at the end of August 2018, in [[Conyers, Georgia|Olde Town Conyers, Georgia]].<ref name="FilmingBegin">{{cite news |url=https://www.rockdalenewtoncitizen.com/news/local/filming-returns-to-olde-town-with-doom-patrol/article_4b801aec-e17d-57cb-af72-a8f0fb34ebd7.html |title=Filming returns to Olde Town with ''Doom Patrol'' |last=Standford |first=Larry |work=[[The Rockdale Citizen]] |date=August 31, 2018 |access-date=September 3, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180904155221/https://www.rockdalenewtoncitizen.com/news/local/filming-returns-to-olde-town-with-doom-patrol/article_4b801aec-e17d-57cb-af72-a8f0fb34ebd7.html |archive-date=September 4, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> Filming continued in Georgia throughout September, in [[Lawrenceville, Georgia|Lawrenceville]] and at [[Briarcliff (mansion)|Briarcliff Mansion]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Walljasper |first1=Matt |title=What's filming in Atlanta now? ''Sextuplets'', ''Doom Patrol'', ''Avengers 4'' (again), and more |url=https://www.atlantamagazine.com/news-culture-articles/whats-filming-in-atlanta-now-sextuplets-doom-patrol-avengers-4-again-and-more/ |website=[[Atlanta (magazine)|Atlanta]] |access-date=September 28, 2018 |date=September 27, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001151826/https://www.atlantamagazine.com/news-culture-articles/whats-filming-in-atlanta-now-sextuplets-doom-patrol-avengers-4-again-and-more/ |archive-date=October 1, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> Principal photography for the first season finished in April 2019.{{Citation needed|date=November 2019}}

Filming for the second season began November 2019 in Georgia.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.exploregeorgia.org/now-filming-in-georgia|title=Now Filming in Georgia|website=Explore Georgia|access-date=November 12, 2019|archive-date=September 25, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190925180041/https://www.exploregeorgia.org/now-filming-in-georgia|url-status=live}}</ref>

Filming for the third season began in January 2021,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://productionlist.com/production/doom-patrol-season-3/|title=Doom Patrol (Season 3)|website=Film & Television Industry Alliance|date=November 23, 2020|access-date=March 10, 2021|archive-date=March 10, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210310195619/https://productionlist.com/production/doom-patrol-season-3/|url-status=live}}</ref> and was wrapped in June.<ref>{{cite web|title=Doom Patrol Wraps Filming on Season 3|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/news/doom-patrol-wraps-filming-season-3-joivan-wade-cyborg-photo/|access-date=July 1, 2021|website=DC|date=June 6, 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

Filming for the fourth season began in February 2022 and was completed in August.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://moviesr.net/p-doom-patrol-season-4-officially-wraps-up-filming-likely-to-release-later-in-2022|title='Doom Patrol' Season 4 Officially Wraps Up Filming, Likely to Release Later in 2022|website=moviesr.net}}</ref>

==Release==
The first season of ''Doom Patrol'' premiered on DC Universe on February 15, 2019,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/robsalkowitz/2018/12/21/dc-universes-live-action-doom-patrol-gets-premiere-date/ |title=DC Universe's Live Action ''Doom Patrol'' Gets Premiere Date |last=Salkowitz |first=Rob |work=Forbes |date=December 21, 2018 |access-date=December 21, 2018 |archive-date=December 21, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181221230628/https://www.forbes.com/sites/robsalkowitz/2018/12/21/dc-universes-live-action-doom-patrol-gets-premiere-date/ |url-status=live}}</ref> with episodes released until May 24.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/10/04/dc-universe-original-release-schedule |title=DC Universe Originals Release Schedule Revealed |last=Ridgely |first=Charlie |work=Comicbook.com |date=October 4, 2018 |access-date=October 13, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181013172317/https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/10/04/dc-universe-original-release-schedule/ |archive-date=October 13, 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> The first season consists of 15 episodes.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/showatch/doom-patrol/listings/ |title=Shows A-Z – ''Doom Patrol'' on DC |work=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=May 17, 2019}}</ref> A second season premiered on both DC Universe and HBO Max on June 25, 2020.<ref name="Goldberg" /> The third season premiered on September 23, 2021, exclusively on HBO Max.<ref name="S3Premiere">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/video/doom-patrol-season-3-premiere-date-trailer-hbo-max/|title='Doom Patrol': HBO Max Unveils Season 3 Premiere Date & Trippy Teaser|work=Deadline Hollywood|first=Alexandra|last=Del Rosario|date=August 9, 2021|access-date=August 9, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210809170620/https://deadline.com/video/doom-patrol-season-3-premiere-date-trailer-hbo-max/|archive-date=August 9, 2021|url-status=live}}</ref> The first half of the fourth season premiered on December 8, 2022, with the first two episodes of the season available immediately and the rest debuting on a weekly basis on HBO Max.<ref name="S4Premiere">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/10/doom-patrol-season-4-trailer-hbo-max-premiere-date-additional-episodes-1235139534/|title='Doom Patrol' Season 4 Trailer: HBO Max Announces Premiere Date Plus Additional Episodes|work=Deadline Hollywood|first=Armando|last=Tinoco|date=October 9, 2022|access-date=October 9, 2022|archive-date=October 9, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221009211050/https://deadline.com/2022/10/doom-patrol-season-4-trailer-hbo-max-premiere-date-additional-episodes-1235139534/|url-status=live}}</ref> The second half of the fourth season premiered on October 12, 2023 with the first two episodes, and the rest debuting on a weekly basis on Max until the series concluded on November 9.<ref name="Season4BTVLine">{{cite web |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/doom-patrol-final-season-4b-release-date-trailer-series-finale-1235046924/ |title=Doom Patrol Sets End Date: Watch Trailer for DC Series' Final 6 Episodes |work=TVLine |first=Ryan |last=Schwartz |date=September 21, 2023 |access-date=September 22, 2023}}</ref>

In the United Kingdom, the first season was released exclusively on StarzPlay on January 2, 2020.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://advanced-television.com/2019/11/21/doom-patrol-finds-uk-home-on-starzplay/|title=Doom Patrol finds UK home on StarzPlay|first=Nik|last=Roseveare|work=Advanced Television Ltd|date=November 21, 2019|access-date=June 10, 2020|archive-date=November 15, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115212019/https://advanced-television.com/2019/11/21/doom-patrol-finds-uk-home-on-starzplay/|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season premiered on July 16, 2021,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/sci-fi/doom-patrol-amazon-prime-video-uk/|title=How to watch DC's Doom Patrol and when it arrives in the UK|website=Radio Times}}</ref> while the third season premiered on November 14 in the same year.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://presskit.lionsgateplus.com/uk/|title=UK}}</ref>

In Australia, the series is streamed on the Australian streaming service [[Binge (streaming service)|Binge]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://binge.com.au/shows/show-doom-patrol!1361|title=Doom Patrol – WATCH ON BINGE|via=[[Binge (streaming service)|Binge]]|access-date=September 2, 2021}}</ref>

==Reception==
===Critical response===
{{Television critical response|rotten_tomatoes1=96% (53 reviews)<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/doom_patrol/s01 |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 1 (2019) |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Fandango Media|Fandango]] |access-date=November 18, 2022}}{{cbignore}}</ref>|metacritic1=70 (18 reviews)<ref name="Doom Patrol: Season 1">{{cite web |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 1 |url=https://www.metacritic.com/tv/doom-patrol |website=[[Metacritic]] |publisher=[[CBS Interactive]] |access-date=November 18, 2022}}{{cbignore}}</ref>|rotten_tomatoes2=97% (29 reviews)<ref name="RT2" />|rotten_tomatoes3=100% (10 reviews)<ref name="RT3" />|rotten_tomatoes4=100% (12 reviews)<ref name="RT4" />}}On review aggregator [[Rotten Tomatoes]], the first season holds a 96% approval rating based on 53 reviews, with an average rating of 8/10. The website's critical consensus reads: "DC Universe finds breakout material in this iteration of ''Doom Patrol'' thanks to a fully committed cast and the writing's faith in weirdness."<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/doom_patrol/s01 |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 1 (2019) |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Fandango Media|Fandango]] |access-date=November 18, 2022}}{{cbignore}}</ref> [[Metacritic]], which uses a [[weighted mean|weighted average]], assigned the series a score of 70 out of 100 based on reviews from 18 critics, indicating "generally favorable reviews".<ref name="Doom Patrol: Season 1">{{cite web |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 1 |url=https://www.metacritic.com/tv/doom-patrol |website=[[Metacritic]] |publisher=[[CBS Interactive]] |access-date=November 18, 2022}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

Jesse Schedeen of [[IGN]] rated the series premiere 9.0 out of 10, praising its "wicked" sense of humor and the show's cast that "works incredibly well to form an entertaining dysfunctional family".<ref>{{cite web |date=February 16, 2019 |first=Jesse |last=Schedeen |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2019/02/16/doom-patrol-season-1-premiere-pilot-review |title=''Doom Patrol'' – Review |website=[[IGN]] |access-date=April 1, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115212010/https://www.ign.com/articles/2019/02/16/doom-patrol-season-1-premiere-pilot-review |url-status=live}}</ref>

The second season holds a 97% approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes, based on 29 reviews with an average rating of 8.3/10. Its critical consensus reads: "As entertaining as the first, but with more emotional depth, ''Doom Patrol''{{'}}s second season explores darker corners without sacrificing any of its wonderful weirdness."<ref name="RT2">{{cite web |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/doom_patrol/s02 |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 2 (2020) |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Fandango Media|Fandango]] |access-date=November 18, 2022}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

The third season has a 100% approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes, based on 10 reviews with an average rating of 7.9/10. Its critics consensus states: "By adding strange new spices and a heaping tablespoon of unconventional plotting, ''Doom Patrol'' remains an endearing bazaar of absurd delights."<ref name="RT3">{{cite web |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/doom_patrol/s03 |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 3 (2021) |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Fandango Media|Fandango]] |access-date=October 24, 2021}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

The fourth and final season has received a 100% approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes, based on 12 reviews with an average rating of 7.5/10. Its critics consensus states: "A dream team of DC Universe misfits take a worthy final bow in a fourth and final season that stays true to its perverse and quirky heart."<ref name="RT4">{{cite web |title=''Doom Patrol'': Season 4 (2022) |url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/doom_patrol/s04 |access-date=November 3, 2023 |website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] |publisher=[[Fandango Media|Fandango]]}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

