==Further media==
===''Titans''===
{{main|Titans (2018 TV series)}}
[[Elasti-Girl|Rita Farr]], [[Negative Man|Larry Trainor]], and [[Robotman (Cliff Steele)|Cliff Steele]] from the ''Doom Patrol'' continuity were intended to appear in the original [[Titans (season 1)|season 1]] finale of ''[[Titans (2018 TV series)|Titans]]''. The appearances were removed after the original season finale was pulled.<ref name="TitansOSF1">{{cite web |last1=Elvy |first1=Craig |title=Titans: What Originally Happened In The Cancelled Season 1 Finale |url=https://screenrant.com/titans-dc-cancelled-season-1-finale-what-happened/ |website=[[Screen Rant]] |access-date=July 2, 2020 |date=November 19, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115211935/https://screenrant.com/titans-dc-cancelled-season-1-finale-what-happened/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title='Titans': Here's What Was Supposed To Happen In The Scrapped Season 1 Finale! |url=https://thegww.com/titans-heres-what-was-supposed-to-happen-in-the-scrapped-season-1-finale/ |website=GWW |access-date=July 2, 2020 |date=November 17, 2019 |archive-date=November 15, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115211936/https://thegww.com/titans-heres-what-was-supposed-to-happen-in-the-scrapped-season-1-finale/ |url-status=live |last1=Kaya |first1=Emre }}</ref>

The ''Titans'' version of [[Cyborg (DC Comics)|Cyborg]] appears in the [[Titans (season 4)|season 4]] episodes "Dude, Where's My Gar" and "Game Over", with [[Joivan Wade]] reprising the role.

===Arrowverse===
{{main|Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)}}
The ''Doom Patrol'' incarnations of [[Crazy Jane|Jane]], Rita Farr, Vic Stone, Larry Trainor, and Cliff Steele make cameo appearances in the [[Arrowverse]] [[crossover (fiction)|crossover]] event "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]", which depicts the series as taking place on the world of Earth-21. [[Diane Guerrero]], [[April Bowlby]], Joivan Wade, Matthew Zuk, and Riley Shanahan appear in their respective roles from ''Doom Patrol'' through archival footage.<ref name="Comic-Book">{{cite web|url=https://cosmicbook.news/crisis-green-lantern-superman-arrowverse-reboot|title=Crisis Teases Green Lantern, Superman; Reboots Arrowverse|last=McGloin|first=Matt|date=January 14, 2020|website=Cosmicbook.news|access-date=January 14, 2020|archive-date=November 15, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201115211936/https://cosmicbook.news/crisis-green-lantern-superman-arrowverse-reboot|url-status=live}}</ref>

